Now update _updateRip to spin body continuously with subtle tilt and bob. Current:

```
if (this.rip.pack) {
  if (!rev.active || rev.t < 0.42) {
    this.rip.pack.rotation.y = Math.sin(t * 0.55) * 0.4;
    this.rip.pack.position.y = 0.06 + Math.sin(t * 1.15) * 0.07;
    if (rev.active && rev.t < 0.42) {
      this.rip.pack.rotation.z = Math.sin(rev.t * 70) * 0.045;
      this.rip.pack.position.x = Math.sin(rev.t * 55) * 0.035;
      this.rip.pack.scale.setScalar(1 + rev.t * 0.2);
    }
  }
}
```

Change rotation:
```
const body = this.rip.pack.userData.body || this.rip.pack;
body.rotation.y += dt * 0.6;
body.rotation.x = Math.sin(t * 0.9) * 0.05;
this.rip.pack.position.y = ...
```
For the reveal shake, keep group rotation.z. But `playRipReveal` resets pack.rotation.set(0,0,0) — body angle persists, okay. After reset, wrapper rotation z/x zero.

Potential issue: During rev active t<0.42, body rotation.x tilt set each frame; wrapper z shake. Fine.

Maybe accelerate spin slightly on windup? Not needed; keep simple. Rotation speed 0.6 rad/s => 10.5 sec per turn, smooth.

But subtle tilt around x plus continuous y rotation means the pack tilts relative to its own local x after rotation composition? Euler order XYZ default: rotation x applied... orientation = R_x * R_y * R_z? THREE Euler 'XYZ' means rotation matrix R = Rx * Ry * Rz? Actually applies x then y then z intrinsically... For object, matrix = Rx Ry Rz. With y continuous and x small, looks like a slight tumble—fine.

Also bob existing. Modified block.

